For $0\le i,j<H$, let $$\ell=j\bmod p,\quad d=(j-i-1)\bmod p,
 \qquad
 i'=\frac{i+1+d-\ell}{p}-1,\quad j'=\left\lfloor\frac jp\right\rfloor,
 \qquad 0\le\ell,d<p.$$ Then $i'\ge-1$, and, with the convention $M^0(-1,j')=k^+_{j'+1}$, $$\label{eq:digit-layers}
 \begin{split}
 p^2M^0(i,j)&\equiv E_dM^0(i',j')\pmod p,\\
 p^2Z^0(i,j)&\equiv
 \begin{cases}
 Z^0(\lfloor i/p\rfloor,j'),&i\equiv j\pmod p,\\
 0,&i\not\equiv j\pmod p.
 \end{cases}
 \end{split}$$

Suppose $H/2<p\le H$, and write $K=L-p$ and $J=H-p$. For every central column, by which we mean $$b\le j<\min(p,L),\qquad j\ge J,$$ one has $$\label{eq:central-layer}
 pF_j\in\mathbb Z_p^n,\qquad
 pF_j\equiv-\sum_{0\le\ell<J}\frac{V_\ell}{j-\ell}\pmod p.$$ All denominators $j-\ell$ occurring here are units at $p$.

For $H/2<p\le H$, define $$\begin{aligned}
 R&=K_++(K-A)_++(J-\max(b,K))_+,\\
 S&=(\min(A,K)-b)_+
        +(\min(b,J)-\max(0,K))_+.
\end{aligned}$$ Then every full raw minor, and hence the filtered determinant, satisfies $$\label{eq:odd-two-layer-bound}
 v_p(\Delta_N)\ge-\min(2n,n+R,2R+S).$$

Assume $G\in\mathbb Q$. Along any sequence of positive integers $N\to\infty$ for which $\Delta_N\ne0$, one has $$\label{eq:finite-lower-final}
 \liminf_{N\to\infty}
 \left(\frac{\log|\Delta_N|}{n^2}-\frac12\log2\right)
 \ge -\frac{8609}{4608}
       -\left(\frac12+\frac{505}{4608}\right)\log2
 >-2.29084.$$

Under Equation <a href="#eq:case-condition" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:case-condition">[eq:case-condition]</a>, $$\label{eq:real-first-sheet-bound}
 |\mathcal R_n(x)|\le(1+K_0n)^n
       \mathcal V(1/x)\prod_i|x_i|^g.$$ In particular, the prefactor is $\exp(O(n\log n))$ uniformly in the nodes.

For every distinct nonzero real list in $(-1,1)$, and in particular when Equation <a href="#eq:case-condition" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:case-condition">[eq:case-condition]</a> fails, $$\label{eq:real-second-sheet-bound}
 |\mathcal R_n(x)|\le
 (3/2)^n n^{n/2}2^{-\binom n2}
 \prod_i(1+x_i^2)^{(n-1)/2}|x_i|^{g-(n-1)}.$$ The factor $(3/2)^n n^{n/2}$ is $\exp(O(n\log n))$; the power $2^{-\binom n2}$ is retained in the principal integrand below.

Let $p,v$ be two such sequences, and take $\lambda=0$ in case $\kappa=2$ or any fixed $\lambda\ge0$ in case $\kappa=1$. Uniformly over configurations in the indicated case, $$\begin{aligned}
 &\limsup_{N\to\infty}\ \sup_{\text{case }\kappa}
 \left(\frac{\log\mathcal I_{\kappa,n}}{n^2}
                  -\frac12\log2\right)\notag\\
 &\qquad\le (-1+\alpha+\gamma)\log2
       +\kappa\|p\|_*^2+\frac12\|v\|_*^2\notag\\
 &\qquad\quad+\sup_{\substack{-1\le x<1\\x\ne0}}
       \{W_\kappa(x)+\lambda D(x)-2\kappa T(p,x)-S(v,x)\}\notag\\
 &\qquad\quad+\sup_{0<s<1}\{W_s(s)+2T(v,s)\}.
 \label{eq:energy-dual}
\end{aligned}$$ Consequently the maximum of the right sides for the two cases bounds $$\limsup_{N\to\infty}\left(n^{-2}\log|\Delta_N|-\tfrac12\log2\right).$$ We use $\log0=-\infty$.

For the determinants of Equation <a href="#eq:determinant" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:determinant">[eq:determinant]</a>, $$\label{eq:certified-real-upper}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}\left(\frac{\log|\Delta_N|}{n^2}
                    -\frac12\log2\right)
 \le -2.290939875<-2.2909.$$ The separate bounds for the majorants in cases $\kappa=2$ and $\kappa=1$ are $-2.290939875$ and $-2.296789875$, respectively.
